      ":question/worked-solution": "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=3.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P(3,4,5)$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(3,4).$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(3,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(3,4) & =\\frac{5(3)}{(4)}-5(3)^2(4)+4\\cos(\\pi (4)) \\\\  & =(\\frac{15}{4})+(-180)+(4) \\\\  & =- \\frac{689}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
